o the $x$-axis, and then\n\n- scales the result by a scale factor of $3$ with center of enlargement at the origin.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279666/field-1" "q-279666/field-2" "q-279666/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad47b548-a298-5cc9-8f69-70fee292db5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a0c32ff7-3fa5-5bd0-866b-11a952dc9609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b52485d3-6e1c-5380-b553-22a97070a902" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279667/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-279667/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fbbf96e7-29e6-55d8-aecf-1a6cd13fdc56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9709c073-24f5-5830-a543-7bb550c9046b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279667/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-279667/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f1ff35f2-4dcc-57e9-88e1-86c2cea6eb9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2621664f-2fa9-5409-ae76-15982dc0b04f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279667/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-279667/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279667" :question/id #uuid "74e22ad9-058b-558a-9d64-05f5c7272969" :question/math-academy-id "q-279667" :question/problem "Construct the matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T$ that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it shears the vector by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis, and then\n\n- scales the result by a scale factor of $4$ with center of enlargement at the origin.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279667/field-1" "q-279667/field-2" "q-279667/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad47b548-a298-5cc9-8f69-70fee292db5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279667"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279670/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cd7126f6-cb5d-5c9c-89e6-548689eb2f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279670/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d04e494-40e1-5933-8305-0c99e51ebd93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279670/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-279670/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279670/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "5e787fcb-e5a5-5c27-9e4a-eb8b79b0935a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279670/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "92630c1d-5dea-54f0-bd8f-6fc528507ee7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279670/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-279670/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:ans